#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:2
msgid "Interface hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:4
msgid ""
"Interface hooks are {ref}`hooks <reference-development-supported-snap-"
"hooks>` that can be executed when an {ref}`interface <explanation-interfaces-"
"all-about-interfaces>` is either connected or disconnected via the "
"interface's plugs and slots mechanism. They can be used to read or write "
"attributes from a connection and, for example, acquire new resources, update "
"internal options or update databases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:6
msgid ""
"ⓘ An interface consists of a connection between a plug and a slot. The slot "
"is the provider of the interface while the plug is the consumer, and a slot "
"can support multiple plug connections. For more details, see {ref}`Interface "
"management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:8
msgid "Connect hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:10
msgid ""
"When a plug connects to a slot, the following hooks are executed "
"sequentially *before* the interface connection occurs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:12
msgid "`prepare-plug-<plugname>` for the snap on the plug-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:13
msgid "`prepare-slot-<slotname>` for the snap on the slot-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:15
msgid ""
"After the interface connection has been created and the security permissions "
"have been updated, the following two hooks are then executed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:17
msgid "`connect-slot-<slotname>` for the snap on the slot-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:18
msgid "`connect-plug-<plugname>` for the snap on the plug-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:20
msgid ""
"If an interface connection fails, all changes are undone and an *undo* hook "
"is run for any interface hooks executed prior to the failure. These undo "
"hooks are executed in reverse order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:22
msgid "`disconnect-plug-<plugname>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:23
msgid "`disconnect-slot-<slotname>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:24
msgid "`unprepare-slot-<slotname>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:25
msgid "`unprepare-plug-<plugname>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:27
msgid ""
"Interface hooks can read the attributes of the affected plug and slot by "
"using the *snapctl* command, as defined by the snap's  {ref}`snap.yaml "
"<reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-snap-format>` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:29
msgid "When executed by slot hooks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:30
msgid ""
"`snapctl get :<slotname> <attribute name>` to read attributes of the local "
"slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:31
msgid ""
"`snapctl get --plug :<slotname> <attribute name>` to read attributes of the "
"plug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:33
msgid "When executed by plug hooks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:34
msgid ""
"`snapctl get :<plugname> <attribute name>` to read attributes of local plug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:35
msgid ""
"` snapctl get --slot :<plugname> <attribute name>` to read attributes of the "
"slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:37
msgid ""
"The plug and slot hooks do not know the corresponding slot and plug names on "
"the other end of the connection. For this reason, the above syntax uses `:"
"<slotname>` in the slot hooks and `:<plugname>` in the plug hooks. It's the "
"`--plug` or `--slot` flag that tells *snapctl* which end of the connection "
"to read attributes from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:39
msgid ""
"In addition to the plug and slot attributes defined in *snap.yaml*, `prepare-"
"plug-` and `prepare-slot-` hooks can create attributes dynamically with the "
"*snapctl* command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:41
msgid "In the *prepare-slot-&lt;slotname&gt;* hook:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:42
msgid ""
"`snapctl set :<slotname> slotattribute=value` to create an attribute for the "
"slot side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:44
msgid "In the *prepare-plug-&lt;plugname&gt;* hook:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:45
msgid ""
"`snapctl set :<plugname> plugattribute=value` to create an attribute for the "
"plug side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:47
msgid ""
"Attributes can only be created in *prepare-* hooks, and only as long as "
"their names do not clash with attributes already defined statically in "
"snap.yaml for the given plug/slot. This means overwriting or overloading "
"statically defined attributes is not allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:49
msgid "Disconnect hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:51
msgid ""
"Disconnect hooks are executed upon manual disconnection or automatically "
"when a snap on either end of a connection is completely removed from the "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:53
msgid "Disconnect hooks are executed in the following order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:54
msgid "`disconnect-slot-<slotname>` for the snap on the slot-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:55
msgid "`disconnect-plug-<plugname>` for the snap on the plug-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:57
msgid ""
"Disconnect hooks can read the attributes of both the plug and slot side of "
"the connection via the *snapctl* command, as described in the \"Connect "
"hooks\" section above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:59
msgid ""
"If an interface disconnection fails, an *undo* hook is run for any interface "
"hooks executed prior to the failure and the connection is restored. These "
"undo hooks are executed in reverse order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:61
msgid "`connect-plug-<plugname>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/interface-hooks.md:62
msgid "`connect-slot-<slotname>`"
msgstr ""
